  "result": "Perfect! All 92 tests pass. Here's what I implemented:\n\n**Summary of tier discount changes:**\n\n1. **Added TIER_DISCOUNTS** (`src/customers.js`): Exported a mapping of customer tiers to discount percentages:\n   - gold: 5%\n   - silver: 2.5%\n   - standard: 0%\n\n2. **Updated `createInvoice`** to apply tier-based discounts:\n   - If a line has an explicit `discountPercent` (even 0), it's used\n   - Otherwise, the customer's tier discount is applied\n   - Used `Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty` to distinguish between \"no discount provided\" and \"explicit 0 discount\"\n\n3. **Updated `addLine`** with the same logic:\n   - New lines get the customer's tier discount if no explicit discount is provided\n   - Existing lines keep their discount when qty is incremented\n   - Explicit discounts override tier discounts\n\n4. **Updated existing tests** to account for tier discounts:\n   - Tests using gold-tier customers (C-001) now expect 5% discounts\n   - Tests needing no discounts now use standard-tier customers (C-002)\n\n5. **Added comprehensive tests** for tier discounts covering:\n   - Each tier applying its correct discount (5%, 2.5%, 0%)\n   - Explicit discounts overriding tier discounts\n   - Multiple lines with mixed tier and explicit discounts\n   - Tier discounts in invoice totals calculations\n   - `addLine` applying tier discounts to new lines",
